[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:41. Do You Call That a Hat]
[00:00.940]Passage 41 | 文章四十一
[00:03.660]Do you call that a hat? | 你把那个叫做帽子吗？
[00:08.395]Do you call that a hat? I said to my wife. | “你把那个叫做帽子吗？”我对妻子说。
[00:14.740]You needn't be so rude about it, my wife answered, as she looked at herself in the mirror. | “你没必要这么粗鲁，”我妻子看着镜子里的自己回答道。
[00:22.245]I sat down on one of those modern chairs with holes in it and waited. | 我坐在一把带洞的现代椅子上，等着。
[00:29.025]We had been in the hat shop for half an hour, and my wife was still in front of the mirror. | 我们已经在帽子店里待了半小时，我妻子仍然在镜子前。
[00:36.425]We mustn't buy things we don't need, I remarked suddenly. | “我们不应该买我们不需要的东西，”我突然说道。
[00:42.810]I regretted saying it almost at once. | 我几乎立刻就后悔说了那句话。
[00:47.170]You needn't have said that, my wife answered. | “你没必要说那句话，”我妻子回答道。
[00:51.485]I need not remind you of that terrible tie you bought yesterday. | 我没必要提醒你昨天买的那条糟糕的领带。
[00:57.415]I find it beautiful, I said. | “我觉得它很漂亮，”我说。
[01:01.135]A man can never have too many ties. | 男人永远不嫌领带多。
[01:05.140]And a woman can't have too many hats, she answered. | “女人也永远不嫌帽子多，”她回答道。
[01:11.250]Ten minutes later, we walked out of the shop together. | 十分种后，我们一起走出了商店。
[01:16.305]My wife was wearing a hat that looked like a lighthouse. | 我妻子戴着一顶看起来像灯塔的帽子。